# Response headers Cloudflare Pages adds to the static build.
#
# NEVER ADD A `Cache-Control` RULE FOR `/content/*`.
#
# ADR-0006 decided that a correction rewrites a dated edition file in place and
# bumps `editionVersion`. An `immutable` or long `max-age` header on that path
# would therefore hide a published correction from every reader who already
# holds the earlier copy — a caching choice that silently suppresses the
# correction record section 46 requires be visible. Pages already answers
# `/content/*` with `max-age=0, must-revalidate` and an ETag, which revalidates
# cheaply and still serves a 304, so there is nothing to gain here and a
# correction to lose.
#
# `/assets/*` needs no rule either. Vite fingerprints those filenames by content
# and the service worker precaches them by that name, so a changed asset is a
# changed URL and the HTTP envelope never has to express the difference.
#
# One rule, for one file whose media type is worth stating rather than
# inferring.
/manifest.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json
